# SPA fallback: every path boots the Blazor router, which renders its own
# NotFound UI for unknown addresses. The tradeoff is that unknown paths
# return 200 instead of 404. Search engines call that a soft 404.
# Cloudflare Pages cannot tell valid client routes (/history, /plan) from
# invalid ones without a Function router, so a 404 rewrite would return 404
# for valid deep links too. 404.html mirrors index.html so removing this
# rule later still renders the app shell with a 404 status.
/* /index.html 200
